From 1210829cff55c85bab901a9381399c569854992e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dyatz <Codename-riho@github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:49:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: optimize multi-manager support and spoofed manager handling

Trust a list of manager signatures (KSUN, pershoot, KOWSU, MamboSU,
Ksu, SukiSU, BakaSU/ReSukiSU) and allow multiple verified managers
to be crowned concurrently (default cap 8, configurable via KSU_MAX_MANAGERS).

- apk_sign.c: raise CERT_MAX_LENGTH to 4096 with kmalloc instead of
  stack allocation, avoid __always_inline stack bloat on
  get_v2_certificate(), and cache KSU_NEXT_MANAGER_LIST as raw 32-byte
  SHA-256 digests under a mutex so /data/app scans match with memcmp()
- manager_identity.h: default KSU_MAX_MANAGERS to 8 (clamped 1..16),
  match uid % KSU_PER_USER_RANGE across all users by default so spoofed
  managers in Work Profile / Private Space / Dual Apps are recognized
  (opt-in KSU_MANAGER_OWNER_ONLY=1), fast-path non-app UIDs before the
  slot loop, and normalize user-prefixed UIDs consistently
- throne_tracker.c: single-pass uid_list pruning + order-independent
  uid_list hash so package swaps (unchanged pkg_count) trigger rescans,
  skip redundant stat/remember for already-tracked APKs, and allow
  root-requested managers (CHANGE_MANAGER_UID) to persist across rescans
  until uninstalled or upgraded to an APK-verified slot
- supercall.c: allow root (uid 0) CHANGE_MANAGER_UID to crown a valid
  app UID via ksu_manager_request() for custom-signed spoofed managers
- dispatch.c: GET_MANAGER_APPID returns the caller's own app id when
  crowned
- allowlist.c: skip umount for any crowned manager
- Kbuild: extended signature list, configurable KSU_MAX_MANAGERS and
  KSU_MANAGER_OWNER_ONLY, do not pin KSU_MANAGER_PACKAGE
